 leaned about eight points Republican, against Democrat Chris Jones. Hill holds the structural advantages: incumbency, roughly $1.4 million more cash on hand, and outside-group support, and eight of ten professional ratings call the race Likely Republican.\n\nThe race is nonetheless closer than the district's lean alone suggests. A Democratic-tilted national environment offsets much of that edge, Jones has raised a competitive $1.8 million, and the one independent poll, Hendrix College in August, showed Jones ahead by four points. Prediction markets still give Hill about an 80 percent chance, and a late Republican complaint over Jones's financial disclosures has added friction. The expected outcome is a narrow Republican win, with above-average uncertainty because the polling is thin and two months old.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1835, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3233, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2423, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2933, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3205, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3445, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2683, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2648, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2693, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2035, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2922, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2948, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1951, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2153, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2896, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2594, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem":